                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "30bd0fec-f2ce-3ea2-a13a-ee63dc76b7cd",
                        "entry_id": "540a3300-8c53-39ba-8f72-6ef5c1f7e4dd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Utilisation de rétronyme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eea59128-f338-4f23-b577-9e61f6d45c13",
                                "sense_id": "30bd0fec-f2ce-3ea2-a13a-ee63dc76b7cd",
                                "text": "Dans la conscience collective, ce n’est que pendant la guerre de 1939-45, par rétronymie (le fait de renommer un objet, un concept ou un événement suite à l’apparition d'une nouvelle information), que la guerre de 1914-1918 devient la « Première Guerre mondiale », et que l’« après-guerre, période s’ouvrant le 11 novembre 1918, devient « l’entre-deux-guerre » en se clôturant le 3 septembre 1939."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "639f7c1b-ec08-469e-a615-11a438be5ff3",
                        "source_entry_id": "540a3300-8c53-39ba-8f72-6ef5c1f7e4dd",
                        "source_sense_id": "30bd0fec-f2ce-3ea2-a13a-ee63dc76b7cd",
                        "target_lang_word": "retronymy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "retronymy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2e15ae7-938b-34e0-a568-35274a3539e1",
                                        "entry_id": "dbcc7631-986b-32d0-8c6a-d725c46a2b13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The process of creating retronyms; coining new words for existing concepts because the meaning of the original word has broadened."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bdc7615b-ad65-4fe3-ba6c-c864d64fc9af",
                                                "sense_id": "d2e15ae7-938b-34e0-a568-35274a3539e1",
                                                "text": "Much retronymy is driven by advances in technology."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9e6eb6d-e570-4e03-b81e-f339489af4e4",
                                                "sense_id": "d2e15ae7-938b-34e0-a568-35274a3539e1",
                                                "text": "Of special interest to terminologists is retronymy, which consists of renaming an existing concept more precisely in order to adjust to a conceptual shift, as will be illustrated below."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf9f74dd-8bab-480b-83c0-9111a2df135f",
                                                "sense_id": "d2e15ae7-938b-34e0-a568-35274a3539e1",
                                                "text": "What they describe is the well-known phenomenon of retronymy (see, for instance, Ahmad & Collingham 1996). Whatever such consequential terminological changes are called, this understanding of 'gap' is system-related."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
